1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,340
How many of us are really sure what's in
Antarctica?

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:11,060
This map from 1513 shows a continent no
one saw until 1820... or does it?

3
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:14,880
Ottoman admiral Piri Reis drew it on
gazelle skin.

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,880
It surfaced in 1929, in Topkapı Palace.

5
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:25,260
Writers saw Antarctica in its southern coast, mapped
before the ice by a lost civilization.

6
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,320
But that ice is millions of years old.

7
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:33,020
Historians see South America there, bent
east to fit the skin.

8
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:38,500
His sources? His notes list about twenty
maps, one drawn by Columbus.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,620
His uncle, the corsair Kemal Reis, held a captive
who sailed with Columbus three times.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,380
He copied the old maps' wonders too:

11
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:53,120
monks on a giant fish, one-horned oxen,
monsters seven spans long.

12
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,480
He even noted... "But they are harmless
souls."

13
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,540
Columbus's own map was never found.

14
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:03,600
And under that ice lie fossil forests,
even dinosaurs.

15
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,780
We still know so little about
Antarctica...

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,980
so how can we be so sure?
